Syntax: who
Syntax: who --brief
Syntax: who --admin
Syntax: who <name>
Syntax: who --help

The who command displays all players who are currently connected.

With no arguments, it lists everyone along with their level, class, race,
and current area. Immortals are shown with their rank and title, colorized
by their power level.

who --brief    Shows only player names and titles, with no mechanical
               information. Useful if you prefer a less spoilery view.

who <name>     Shows detailed information about a specific player including
               their title, level, class, race, area, group members, and
               how long they have been online. Also matches abbreviations,
               so "who joe" would match "Joe", "Joey", and "JoeBlow".

who --admin    (Immortal only) Shows detailed admin info for all players
               including idle time, hit points, mana/piety/lifeforce,
               movement, and account names.

who --help     Displays a quick summary of available options.

Tags such as (Seeking Group), (Newbie-Helper), and (Newbie) will appear
next to player names when applicable.


